course: dictionary
lesson: 10117
title: The thorax
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Look at a bee or a fly and you will see three main parts: a head, a thorax and an abdomen. The thorax is the middle part, between the head and the abdomen. «An insect's body has a head, a thorax and an abdomen.»
explain: The thorax is where the legs and wings are fixed. «Every adult insect has six legs and a body in three parts; the legs and wings are all fixed to the thorax.» So if you want to find an insect's legs, look at its thorax.
explain: Animals with backbones, like you, have a thorax too, but it means something a little different. In people, the thorax is your chest: the part of the body between your neck and your belly. It holds your heart and lungs.
fact: Thorax is a noun. In insects it is the middle body part; in people it is the chest.
fact: The plural of thorax can be thoraxes or thoraces.
fact: An insect has three body parts: head, thorax and abdomen.
fact: Every adult insect has six legs, and all six are joined to the thorax.
fact: Spiders are not insects: they have two body parts and eight legs.
exercise: «An insect's body has a head, a thorax and an abdomen.» What is the thorax? | The chest of a bird | Its head with the eyes and feelers | *The middle part of the body, between the head and the abdomen | The back end of the body
exercise: Where are an insect's legs fixed? | To the feelers | To the head | *To the thorax | To the abdomen
exercise: «Spiders have eight legs and two body parts.» How many body parts does a spider have? | *Two | Three | Six | Four
test: Which part of your body is the same kind of part as an insect's thorax? | Your fingers | Your knee | Your head | *Your chest, between your neck and your belly
test: «A caterpillar has six true legs at the front.» How many true legs does a caterpillar have? | Eight | Twelve | Four | *Six
exam: A ladybird is an insect. Which body parts does it have? | Head and legs only | *Head, thorax and abdomen | Head and thorax only | Head and abdomen only
